{ L"A circle's area and its circumference have the same numeric value. What is its radius?", 2, L"Set \u03C0r\u00B2 = 2\u03C0r and divide both sides by \u03C0r: r = 2." },
{ L"Each interior angle of a regular polygon measures 140 degrees. How many sides does the polygon have?", 9, L"Each exterior angle is 180 \u2212 140 = 40 degrees, and exterior angles always sum to 360, so there are 360/40 = 9 sides." },
{ L"Every edge of a cube is made 3 times as long. By what factor does the cube's volume grow?", 27, L"Volume scales with the cube of the length factor: 3\u00B3 = 27." },
{ L"A cone and a cylinder have the same base and the same height. The cylinder holds 90 liters. How many liters does the cone hold?", 30, L"A cone holds exactly one third of the cylinder with the same base and height: 90/3 = 30." },
{ L"A right triangle has legs of length 20 and 21. How long is its hypotenuse?", 29, L"20\u00B2 + 21\u00B2 = 400 + 441 = 841, and \u221A841 = 29." },
{ L"Two angles of a triangle measure 47 and 68 degrees. In degrees, what is the exterior angle at the third vertex?", 115, L"An exterior angle equals the sum of the two opposite interior angles: 47 + 68 = 115." },
{ L"A rectangle has a diagonal of length 13 and a perimeter of 34. What is its area?", 60, L"a + b = 17 and a\u00B2 + b\u00B2 = 169, so 2ab = 17\u00B2 \u2212 169 = 120 and ab = 60." },
{ L"The space diagonal of a cube, from one corner to the opposite corner, has length 6\u221A3. What is the cube's volume?", 216, L"A cube with edge a has space diagonal a\u221A3, so a = 6 and the volume is 6\u00B3 = 216." },
{ L"A ball fits exactly inside a cube with edge length 6, touching all six faces. The ball's volume is k\u03C0. What is k?", 36, L"The ball's diameter equals the edge, so r = 3 and V = (4/3)\u03C0 \u00D7 3\u00B3 = 36\u03C0." },
{ L"Points A, B and C lie on a circle. The arc AB that does not contain C measures 110 degrees. In degrees, what is angle ACB?", 55, L"An inscribed angle is half the arc it cuts off: 110/2 = 55." },
{ L"A 4\u00D74\u00D74 cube is painted on the outside and cut into 64 unit cubes. How many unit cubes have exactly two painted faces?", 24, L"Two-face cubes sit on the edges but not at the corners: each of the 12 edges has 4 \u2212 2 = 2 of them, so 24." },
{ L"A circle is inscribed in a right triangle with legs 8 and 15. What is the radius of the circle?", 3, L"The hypotenuse is 17, and in a right triangle r = (a + b \u2212 c)/2 = (8 + 15 \u2212 17)/2 = 3." },
{ L"A triangle has sides of length 13, 14 and 15. What is its area?", 84, L"The altitude to side 14 has length 12 and splits it into 5 and 9 (5-12-13 and 9-12-15). Area = 14 \u00D7 12 / 2 = 84." },
{ L"A square is inscribed in a circle, and a second square is circumscribed around the same circle. The inner square has area 50. What is the outer square's area?", 100, L"The circle's diameter is the inner square's diagonal and the outer square's side. Side d gives area d\u00B2, diagonal d gives d\u00B2/2, so 2 \u00D7 50 = 100." },
{ L"A rope hugs a planet's equator. It is lengthened just enough to float 5 m above the ground all the way around. The added length is k\u03C0 m. What is k?", 10, L"Circumference is 2\u03C0r, so raising the radius by 5 adds 2\u03C0 \u00D7 5 = 10\u03C0, whatever the planet's size." },
{ L"A regular hexagon has side length 2. Its area can be written as k\u221A3. What is k?", 6, L"A regular hexagon is 6 equilateral triangles of side 2, each with area \u221A3, so the total is 6\u221A3." },
{ L"In a right triangle, the altitude to the hypotenuse divides it into pieces of length 4 and 9. How long is that altitude?", 6, L"The altitude to the hypotenuse is the geometric mean of the two pieces: \u221A(4 \u00D7 9) = 6." },
{ L"Ten people each shake hands with every other person exactly once. How many handshakes take place?", 45, L"Each handshake is a pair of people: 10 \u00D7 9 / 2 = 45." },
{ L"In how many different orders can 5 people stand in a line?", 120, L"5 choices for the first spot, 4 for the next, and so on: 5 \u00D7 4 \u00D7 3 \u00D7 2 \u00D7 1 = 120." },
{ L"A pizzeria offers 6 toppings. How many different pizzas can be made with exactly 2 different toppings?", 15, L"Order does not matter, so count pairs: 6 \u00D7 5 / 2 = 15." },
{ L"You walk from (0, 0) to (4, 4) on a street grid, each step one block east or one block north. How many different routes are there?", 70, L"Every route has 8 steps, 4 of them east. Choose which 4: C(8,4) = 70." },
{ L"How many distinct arrangements are there of the letters in the word LEVEL?", 30, L"The 5 letters have 120 orders; divide by 2 for the two L's and by 2 for the two E's: 120/4 = 30." },
{ L"How many squares of any size are outlined by the lines of a 4 by 4 grid of unit squares?", 30, L"Sizes 1 to 4 give 4\u00B2, 3\u00B2, 2\u00B2 and 1\u00B2 squares: 16 + 9 + 4 + 1 = 30." },
{ L"How many rectangles of any size, squares included, are outlined by the lines of a 3 by 3 grid of unit squares?", 36, L"A rectangle is fixed by choosing 2 of the 4 vertical lines and 2 of the 4 horizontal lines: 6 \u00D7 6 = 36." },
{ L"Gold, silver and bronze medals go to 3 of 8 runners, with no ties. How many different medal outcomes are possible?", 336, L"8 choices for gold, then 7 for silver, then 6 for bronze: 8 \u00D7 7 \u00D7 6 = 336." },
{ L"Choose 3 of the 8 vertices of a cube. For how many of the possible choices do the 3 points form a triangle?", 56, L"No three vertices of a cube lie on one line, so every choice works: C(8,3) = 56." },
{ L"How many 4-digit numbers have digits that strictly increase from left to right, like 1357?", 126, L"Pick any 4 different digits from 1 to 9 (0 would have to lead); they sort in exactly one way: C(9,4) = 126." },
{ L"Four letters are placed at random into their four addressed envelopes, one each. Of the 24 possible ways, how many put no letter in its own envelope?", 9, L"Letter A has 3 wrong envelopes to go into, and each choice leaves exactly 3 ways to place the rest with no match: 3 \u00D7 3 = 9." },
{ L"Five straight lines are drawn in a plane, no two parallel and no three through one point. Into how many regions do they divide the plane?", 16, L"The k-th line crosses the k \u2212 1 earlier lines and so adds k new regions: 1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 16." },
{ L"In how many ways can a 2 by 8 rectangle be tiled with eight 1 by 2 dominoes?", 34, L"The left end is one vertical domino or two stacked flat ones, so the counts follow Fibonacci: 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 34." },
{ L"How many pairs of squares on an 8 by 8 chessboard share a side?", 112, L"Each row has 7 side-by-side pairs and each column has 7 stacked pairs: 8 \u00D7 7 + 8 \u00D7 7 = 112." },
{ L"Five people sit around a round table. Seatings that differ only by a rotation count as the same. How many different seatings are there?", 24, L"Fix one person's seat to remove rotations, then arrange the other 4: 4 \u00D7 3 \u00D7 2 \u00D7 1 = 24." },
{ L"A committee of 3 is chosen from 5 women and 4 men. How many possible committees include at least one woman?", 80, L"All committees minus the all-male ones: C(9,3) \u2212 C(4,3) = 84 \u2212 4 = 80." },
{ L"In how many ways can 8 identical coins be shared among 3 people so that each person gets at least one coin?", 21, L"Line up the 8 coins and place 2 dividers in the 7 gaps between them: C(7,2) = 21." },
{ L"Two fair dice are rolled. Out of the 36 equally likely outcomes, how many give a sum of 7?", 6, L"(1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1): every first roll has exactly one partner." },
{ L"Two fair dice are rolled. Out of the 36 equally likely outcomes, how many show at least one 6?", 11, L"Count the opposite: 5 \u00D7 5 = 25 outcomes have no 6, so 36 \u2212 25 = 11." },
{ L"On average, how many rolls of a fair six-sided die does it take to get the first 6?", 6, L"Each roll succeeds with chance 1/6, and the average wait for an event of chance p is 1/p = 6 rolls." },
{ L"Three fair coins are tossed. Out of the 8 equally likely outcomes, how many show exactly two heads?", 3, L"Choose which 2 of the 3 coins are heads: HHT, HTH, THH, so 3." },
{ L"Two fair dice are rolled. Out of the 36 equally likely outcomes, how many give an even product?", 27, L"A product is odd only if both dice are odd: 3 \u00D7 3 = 9. The other 36 \u2212 9 = 27 are even." },
{ L"Five fair coins are tossed. The chance that all five land the same way up is 1 in how many?", 16, L"Of the 32 outcomes, only all heads and all tails qualify: 2/32 = 1/16." },
{ L"A bag holds 3 red and 2 blue balls. Two are drawn without replacement. The chance that both are red is k in 10. What is k?", 3, L"3/5 for the first red, then 2/4 for the second: 3/5 \u00D7 2/4 = 6/20 = 3/10." },
{ L"You flip a fair coin until you have seen at least one head and at least one tail. On average, how many flips does that take?", 3, L"The first flip is free; then you wait for the opposite side, which takes 2 flips on average: 1 + 2 = 3." },
{ L"One card is drawn from a standard 52-card deck. The chance that it is a heart or a king (or both) is k in 52. What is k?", 16, L"13 hearts plus 4 kings, minus the king of hearts counted twice: 13 + 4 \u2212 1 = 16." },
{ L"Two fair dice, one red and one blue, are rolled. Out of the 36 equally likely outcomes, in how many does red show more than blue?", 15, L"6 outcomes are ties; by symmetry the other 30 split evenly between red higher and blue higher: 15." },
{ L"A fair die is rolled three times. Out of the 216 equally likely outcomes, in how many are the three results strictly increasing?", 20, L"Pick 3 different values; they have exactly one increasing order: C(6,3) = 20." },
{ L"On average, how many flips of a fair coin does it take to get two heads in a row?", 6, L"Let E be the answer. T restarts, HT restarts, HH ends: E = (E + 1)/2 + (E + 2)/4 + 2/4, so E/4 = 3/2 and E = 6." },
{ L"A deck of 52 cards is shuffled uniformly at random. On average, how many cards end up in their original position?", 1, L"Each card stays put with chance 1/52, and averages add: 52 \u00D7 1/52 = 1." },
{ L"A shuffled pile has 3 aces and 16 other cards. On average, at what position from the top does the first ace appear (top card = position 1)?", 5, L"The 3 aces split the 16 other cards into 4 gaps of 4 cards on average, so the first ace follows 4 cards, at position 5." },
{ L"A stick is broken at two points chosen uniformly at random. The chance that the three pieces can form a triangle is 1 in how many?", 4, L"With a stick of length 1, every piece must be under 1/2. Plotting the two cut points, that region fills 1/4 of the square." },
{ L"Four people each pick a whole number from 1 to 4 at random. Out of the 256 equally likely outcomes, how many have all four numbers different?", 24, L"The first person has 4 options, the next 3, then 2, then 1: 4 \u00D7 3 \u00D7 2 \u00D7 1 = 24." },
{ L"A fair coin is flipped 10 times. The chance of getting exactly 5 heads is k in 1024. What is k?", 252, L"Choose which 5 of the 10 flips are heads: C(10,5) = 252." },
{ L"If x + y = 13 and x \u2212 y = 7, what is x\u00B2 \u2212 y\u00B2?", 91, L"x\u00B2 \u2212 y\u00B2 = (x + y)(x \u2212 y) = 13 \u00D7 7 = 91, with no need to find x and y." },
{ L"What is log base 4 of 1024?", 5, L"1024 = 2^10 = (2\u00B2)^5 = 4^5, so the log is 5." },
{ L"What is the sum of the first 50 odd numbers, 1 + 3 + 5 + \u2026 + 99?", 2500, L"The first n odd numbers always add up to n\u00B2: 50\u00B2 = 2500." },
{ L"Two numbers have a sum of 20 and a product of 91. What is the larger of the two?", 13, L"The numbers are roots of t\u00B2 \u2212 20t + 91 = 0, which factors as (t \u2212 7)(t \u2212 13). The larger is 13." },
{ L"If x + 1/x = 4, what is x\u00B2 + 1/x\u00B2?", 14, L"Square both sides: x\u00B2 + 2 + 1/x\u00B2 = 16, so x\u00B2 + 1/x\u00B2 = 14." },
{ L"If 2x + 3y = 23 and 3x + 2y = 22, what is x + y?", 9, L"Add the two equations: 5x + 5y = 45, so x + y = 9." },
{ L"One root of x\u00B2 \u2212 9x + c = 0 is twice the other. What is c?", 18, L"Call the roots r and 2r. Their sum 3r = 9 gives r = 3, and c is their product: 3 \u00D7 6 = 18." },
{ L"If 3^x = 5, what is 9^x?", 25, L"9^x = (3\u00B2)^x = (3^x)\u00B2 = 5\u00B2 = 25." },
{ L"What is 6 + 3 + 3/2 + 3/4 + \u2026, with each term half the previous one, continued forever?", 12, L"A geometric series sums to first term/(1 \u2212 ratio) = 6/(1 \u2212 1/2) = 12." },
{ L"If 2^x = 8^(x \u2212 4), what is x?", 6, L"8 = 2\u00B3, so the right side is 2^(3x \u2212 12). Then x = 3x \u2212 12, giving x = 6." },
{ L"For how many integers n is n\u00B2 \u2212 10n + 21 negative?", 3, L"It factors as (n \u2212 3)(n \u2212 7), which is negative only strictly between 3 and 7: n = 4, 5, 6." },
{ L"If x + 1/x = 3, what is x\u00B3 + 1/x\u00B3?", 18, L"Cube it: (x + 1/x)\u00B3 = x\u00B3 + 1/x\u00B3 + 3(x + 1/x), so 27 = x\u00B3 + 1/x\u00B3 + 9 and the answer is 18." },
{ L"What is the product (log base 2 of 3) \u00D7 (log base 3 of 4) \u00D7 (log base 4 of 5) \u00D7 \u2026 \u00D7 (log base 15 of 16)?", 4, L"Change of base turns each factor into ln(k + 1)/ln k, so the product telescopes to ln 16/ln 2 = 4." },
{ L"A function satisfies f(x) + 2f(1 \u2212 x) = 3x for every real x. What is f(0)?", 2, L"Plug in x = 0 and x = 1: f(0) + 2f(1) = 0 and f(1) + 2f(0) = 3. Solving gives f(1) = \u22121 and f(0) = 2." },
{ L"A function on the integers satisfies f(x + y) = f(x) + f(y) for all integers x and y, and f(3) = 12. What is f(10)?", 40, L"Additivity forces f(n) = n \u00B7 f(1). From f(3) = 12, f(1) = 4, so f(10) = 40." },
{ L"What is the value of \u221A(6 + \u221A(6 + \u221A(6 + \u2026))), nested forever?", 3, L"The expression x reappears inside itself: x = \u221A(6 + x), so x\u00B2 = x + 6, whose positive root is 3." },
{ L"The two roots of x\u00B2 \u2212 7x + 3 = 0 are r and s. What is r\u00B2 + s\u00B2?", 43, L"r + s = 7 and rs = 3, so r\u00B2 + s\u00B2 = (r + s)\u00B2 \u2212 2rs = 49 \u2212 6 = 43." },
{ L"The sum 1/(1\u00D72) + 1/(2\u00D73) + 1/(3\u00D74) + \u2026 + 1/(99\u00D7100) equals k/100. What is k?", 99, L"1/(n(n + 1)) = 1/n \u2212 1/(n + 1), so the sum telescopes to 1 \u2212 1/100 = 99/100." },
{ L"What is the slope of the curve y = x\u00B3 at the point where x = 2?", 12, L"The derivative of x\u00B3 is 3x\u00B2, and at x = 2 that is 3 \u00D7 4 = 12." },
{ L"What is the determinant of the 2\u00D72 matrix with rows (3, 1) and (4, 2)?", 2, L"For rows (a, b) and (c, d) the determinant is ad \u2212 bc = 3 \u00D7 2 \u2212 1 \u00D7 4 = 2." },
{ L"What is \u222B from 0 to 3 of x\u00B2 dx?", 9, L"An antiderivative of x\u00B2 is x\u00B3/3, so the integral is 27/3 \u2212 0 = 9." },
{ L"What is the limit of (x\u00B2 \u2212 9)/(x \u2212 3) as x approaches 3?", 6, L"Factor: x\u00B2 \u2212 9 = (x \u2212 3)(x + 3), so for x \u2260 3 the expression is x + 3, which tends to 6." },
{ L"What is the rank of the 4\u00D74 matrix in which every entry is 1?", 1, L"All four rows are identical, so they span just one direction: rank 1." },
{ L"What is \u222B from \u22121 to 1 of (x\u00B3 + 5x + 3) dx?", 6, L"x\u00B3 + 5x is odd and cancels over [\u22121, 1], leaving the integral of 3 over an interval of length 2: 6." },
{ L"What is the rank of the 3\u00D73 matrix with rows (1, 2, 3), (4, 5, 6) and (7, 8, 9)?", 2, L"Row 3 = 2 \u00D7 row 2 \u2212 row 1, while rows 1 and 2 are not multiples of each other, so the rank is 2." },
{ L"The region between y = x and y = x\u00B2 for x from 0 to 1 has area 1/k. What is k?", 6, L"On [0, 1] the line y = x lies above y = x\u00B2, so the area is \u222B(x \u2212 x\u00B2) dx = 1/2 \u2212 1/3 = 1/6." },
{ L"How many turning points does the graph of f(x) = x\u00B3 \u2212 3x have?", 2, L"The derivative 3x\u00B2 \u2212 3 is zero at x = 1 and x = \u22121 and changes sign at both: 2 turning points." },
{ L"The tangent line to y = x\u00B2 at x = 3 crosses the y-axis at y = \u2212k. What is k?", 9, L"The slope at x = 3 is 2 \u00D7 3 = 6, so the tangent is y = 9 + 6(x \u2212 3) = 6x \u2212 9, crossing the y-axis at \u22129." },
{ L"What is the limit of sin(5x)/x as x approaches 0?", 5, L"Write sin(5x)/x = 5 \u00B7 sin(5x)/(5x); since sin(u)/u \u2192 1, the limit is 5." },
{ L"A 3\u00D73 matrix A has determinant 2. What is the determinant of 2A?", 16, L"Scaling an n\u00D7n matrix by c scales its determinant by c^n: 2\u00B3 \u00D7 2 = 16." },
{ L"What is the determinant of the 3\u00D73 matrix with rows (2, 0, 0), (5, 3, 0) and (7, 1, 4)?", 24, L"The matrix is lower triangular, so the determinant is the product of the diagonal: 2 \u00D7 3 \u00D7 4 = 24." },
{ L"What is the local maximum value of f(x) = x\u00B3 \u2212 12x?", 16, L"The derivative 3x\u00B2 \u2212 12 is zero at x = 2 and x = \u22122. The maximum is at x = \u22122: f(\u22122) = \u22128 + 24 = 16." },
{ L"How many real solutions does the equation x\u00B3 \u2212 3x + 1 = 0 have?", 3, L"The cubic has a local max f(\u22121) = 3 > 0 and a local min f(1) = \u22121 < 0, so it crosses the x-axis 3 times." },
{ L"How many real solutions does the equation e^x = x + 1 have?", 1, L"y = x + 1 is the tangent line to e^x at x = 0, and e^x curves upward, staying above it everywhere else: only x = 0." },
{ L"As n grows without bound, (1 + 2/n)^n approaches e^k. What is k?", 2, L"(1 + 2/n)^n = ((1 + 2/n)^(n/2))\u00B2, and the inner part tends to e, so the limit is e\u00B2." },
{ L"What is the larger eigenvalue of the 2\u00D72 matrix with rows (2, 1) and (1, 2)?", 3, L"The eigenvalues sum to the trace 4 and multiply to the determinant 3, so they are 3 and 1." },
